[
    {
        "content": "<p>The following behaviour is quite funny:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"myFoo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Invalid argument name `m`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Invalid argument name `[anonymous]`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What's happening is that the <code>myFoo m</code> syntax becomes <code>foo (m := m)</code>, which obviously makes no sense, and <code>foo (5 := 5)</code> is even more meaningless. </p>\n<p>Is this considered a bug, or is it \"expected behaviour\" (in the sense that we should just not expect the notation system to be clever enough) ? Of course the obvious fix is to do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"myFoo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 584048417,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1775582658
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would say this is a bug</p>",
        "id": 584048564,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775582705
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my context this was a bit hidden : these implicit parameters were referring to types, and in most of the type the value assigned for the parameter happened to be a variable named like the parameter. So the notation worked well for most of the file, but then suddenly started breaking in more complicated statements.</p>",
        "id": 584048756,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1775582775
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well <code>foo (5 := 5)</code> is not syntax you can normally obtain</p>",
        "id": 584049466,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775582978
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does <code>«n» := n</code> also fix it?</p>",
        "id": 584064651,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1775588184
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>won't that just do the same thing</p>",
        "id": 584065142,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775588366
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah it does the same thing</p>",
        "id": 584065220,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775588393
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the solution obviously is making the notation variable different, i.e. <code>notation \"myFoo\" m =&gt; foo (n := m)</code></p>",
        "id": 584071883,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1775590689
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>turns out, i need to read the thread better. this was already mentioned.</p>",
        "id": 584072010,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1775590733
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my opinion this is expected behavior. Are there instances where <code>notation</code> does anything other than syntactic replacement?</p>\n<p>Consider, for instance, the following contrived example where we <em>want</em> to replace the named arguments:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"myFoo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: 1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Personally, I would be confused if this could not be achieved using <code>notation</code>.</p>",
        "id": 584147492,
        "sender_full_name": "fiforeach",
        "timestamp": 1775632146
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but normally <code>notation</code> only creates valid syntax</p>",
        "id": 584190825,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775644028
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>just checked <code>foo (5 := 5)</code> is definitely <strong>not</strong> valid syntax (<code>5</code> is not an <code>ident</code>)</p>",
        "id": 584190899,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775644054
    }
]